# Stories
# Copy this file to stories.md and fill in your own stories.
# One story = one "## " block with NO blank lines inside (kb_loader splits on
# blank lines, so a blank line would cut the story in half).
# The interview brief maps likely behavioural questions to these titles; the
# cover letter and form answers may draw on them too, so keep them factual.
# Practise each one out loud until it takes about two minutes.

## Fixing a production incident under pressure | <Company> | <Year>
- Question types: hardest bug, working under pressure, ownership
- Situation: <what broke, who was affected, the stakes>
- Task: <what you were responsible for>
- Action: <what you did, step by step, including the dead ends>
- Result: <measurable outcome; what you changed so it cannot happen again>

## Disagreeing with a technical decision | <Company> | <Year>
- Question types: conflict, influencing without authority, receiving feedback
- Situation: <...>
- Task: <...>
- Action: <...>
- Result: <...>

## Learning something new fast | <Company / Project> | <Year>
- Question types: learning, ambiguity, a gap in your experience
- Situation: <...>
- Task: <...>
- Action: <...>
- Result: <...>
